    {
      "id": "6bn38u2",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. BASIC CONCEPT"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Percentage represents a number or ratio expressed as a fraction of 100.",
        "To convert a fraction to a percentage, multiply by 100; to convert a percentage to a fraction, divide by 100.",
        "Successive percentage changes can be calculated using the net percentage change formula: a + b + (ab/100)%.",
        "Reverse percentage techniques are essential for determining original amounts prior to any applied increase or decrease."
      ],
      "id": "nh18nux"
    },
    {
      "id": "1ryhth1",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Percentage means 'per hundred'.<br></br>1% = 1/100",
        "Percentage is used to express increase or decrease, comparison, profit and loss, marks, population, growth, etc.<br></br><br></br><em>In SSC examination, percentage questions are direct, formula-based, and often linked with Ratio, Profit–Loss and Simple Interest.</em>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "nosr9li",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. CONVERSION RULES"
    },
    {
      "id": "x3qnnvg",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Fraction to Percentage:<br></br>(a/b) × 100<br></br>Example: 3/5 = 60%",
        "Percentage to Fraction:<br></br>x% = x/100<br></br>Example: 25% = 1/4",
        "Decimal to Percentage:<br></br>Multiply the decimal by 100<br></br>Example: 0.75 = 75%"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "u6smbdn",
      "type": "heading",
